Z||000000||MooCow||07-17-2000||10:17 PM||||First of all I can't tell you how happy I am at owning a Fiero.<BR>Now I have some questions for you people:<BR>1.) I took out the old deck and put in a 2000 Kenwood CD receiver.  When I turn the car on it won't start or anything until the radio deck turns itself on.  What makes it do that. After the deck is on it starts right up.<BR>2.)What size bulb goes in the parking likes up front under the headlight?  The left is burned out.<BR>3.)The power windows and doors only on the driver's side sticks.  I lubed up the power locks on both sides and it seems to work fine.  The power window only on the driver's side tends not to even work at all.  I took the door off and shook the wires and poof it worked.  It goes of and on.  So I checked all the connectors and they seem okay so do I have a burned wire somewhere or how do I fix this problem??  Remember I have little little little money right now cause I just got it yesterday.<P>                             Thanks  Ken||||reg||5
Z||000001||Seanh||07-17-2000||10:31 PM||||hum....Strange that the car wont start until the cd player turns on. Do this, turn on the key and once the cd player comes on, push the power button and shut it off. Turn off the key and then turn it back on, the cd player shouldnt come on, try and start the car. Do this and tell me what happens. I am a stero installer and I have never herd of this happening. Maybe because I have the only Fiero in town though. Anyway, I am currently unsure of the light number. But if no one else has told you, I am going by the parts store tomarrow and Ill get the number for you there. Sorry but I cant help on the window. I will help ya through the stero problem.<P>------------------<BR>Sean Heberly<BR>Silver 86 GT<BR>2.8 w/Twin Turbos||||reg||1
