Z||000008||Seanh||07-19-2000||11:23 PM||||Sorry, havent been to walmart to pick up film yet. It will be another few days, but Ill get them by the weekend. I really didnt think I was sitting on such a rare fiero, with twins and all. I didnt think it was that uncommon to run twins on a 2.8. Come to think of it, Iv never seen them on a 2.8, I have however on a 3.4 fiero. I think that engine is going here pretty soon to a northstar v8 when I recover from the Pioneer system I put in it.<P>------------------<BR>Sean Heberly<BR>Silver 86 GT 2.8||||reg||1
Z||000009||LarryB||07-20-2000||04:59 AM||||The bulb for the front parking light/turn signal is # 2057.  You use a T-15 Torx screwdriver to remove the 2 screws holding the plastic assembly off then twist the socket to get to the bulb.  Takes a few minutes to do the whole thing.<P>Just be careful when sliding the assembly out, there's enough slack in the wiring so you can get at the socket, but not by much. If you break a wire or the socket has gone bad you can fish the socket through and get at it by lifting the hood and raising the headlight but working space is pretty tight.<BR>||||reg||1
